New opt-in option `--quantified-check-call-facts` (also `quantified-check-call-facts = true` in a project file). With it, when a method postcondition or the condition of an `assert` statement is a universal quantifier, the checked body of the quantifier has the call facts of the functions it calls as its antecedent, so that a function's definition is still available where the solver simplifies the body until no trigger term remains. For example, `ensures forall i | 0 <= i < |l| :: abs(l[i] - l[i]) <= d` now verifies for a `d >= 0.0`. The quantifier assumed after the check is the original one. Without the option, verification is unchanged.
